$DIR/main.p:12:25: an or statement cannot be the post statement of a for statement; test the error in the loop body
    The post statement of a for statement runs at the end of each iteration. An
    or statement cannot be the post statement, since a break or continue in its
    clause would end or repeat the iteration that is ending.
    Test the error at the end of the loop body instead.
    Test the error in the body:
        for i := 0; i < n; {
            ...
            i = next(i) or break
        }
    (see "Or clauses" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.27)
    (run "pluto explain E2465" for a longer explanation)

